## Architecture

The app follows **Feature-Based Architecture (Screaming Architecture)**. All related code lives together grouped by business domain (feature), not by technical concern (components, hooks, etc.).

There are no broad `src/services/` or `src/utils/` folders mapping to the entire application.

```
src/
├── app/               # Next.js App Router (pages and api routes only)
├── features/          # Business feature modules (where the actual code lives)
│   ├── [feature-a]/
│   ├── [feature-b]/
│   └── shared/        # Cross-cutting UI, types, and hooks used by 3+ features
├── lib/               # Framework integrations (Prisma client, Auth, api/client)
└── ...
```

---

## Feature Structure

Every feature lives in `src/features/<feature>/` with this exact layout:

```
src/features/<feature>/
├── components/       # React components (Server and Client)
├── hooks/            # Custom hooks for the feature
├── lib/              # Feature-specific libraries (Zod schemas, API client wrappers)
│   ├── <feature>-api.ts
│   └── <feature>-schemas.ts
├── types/            # TypeScript interfaces and types
├── services/         # Prisma queries & domain logic (Server-only)
├── mappers/          # Data mappers (DTO to domain, optional)
└── __tests__/        # Colocated tests for this feature
    ├── lib/
    ├── hooks/
    ├── mappers/
    └── fixtures/     # Test data and Prisma object mocks
```

